# This is developed on Windows and runs on Linux. A shell script that reaches a Raspberry Pi
# with CRLF endings fails as "cannot execute: required file not found", because the \r becomes
# part of the interpreter path in the shebang — a confusing error for a whitespace problem.
*.sh        text eol=lf
# csi_node.py is copied onto a Pi and marked executable, so its shebang has the same problem.
pi/*.py     text eol=lf
Containerfile text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
# The self-hosted webfonts. Marked so a Windows checkout cannot decide these are text and
# rewrite line endings inside them, which corrupts the file for no visible reason.
*.woff2     binary
